Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::a_card_specific_data_decode_is_total_and_never_overflows`.

The defect: a high-capacity (structure 1) card reads the 28-bit size field of an ultra-capacity
card, so a stranger's register can claim up to 2^38 blocks where the field is 22 bits wide, and the
range check then admits blocks the card does not have.

Expected to fail: the harness's structure 1 bound, `sd.blocks <= 1 << 32`.

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/card.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/card.rs
index 552a189bb..2dbbc5251 100644
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/card.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/card.rs
@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@ impl CardSpecificData {
                 }
             }
             // (C_SIZE + 1) * 512 KiB, C_SIZE 22 bits.
-            1 => (bits(register, 48, 22) as u64 + 1) * 1024,
+            1 => (bits(register, 48, 28) as u64 + 1) * 1024,
             // SDUC: the same, C_SIZE 28 bits.
             2 => (bits(register, 48, 28) as u64 + 1) * 1024,
             _ => 0,
